I go down and fetch the caretaker.
He comes up into the flat with me.
"It is very cold," I say.
He walks over to the window.
He feels it.
He looks at the radiator.
Then he turns up the heat.
It only takes a moment.
I can hear the water inside it.
Soon it grows warm.
"There you go," he says.
"The heat works now."
I feel the radiator.
Now it is warm.
"Thank you so much!" I say, relieved.
He leaves, and I take off my coat.
